.Dd $Mdocdate: May 16 2026 $
.Dt UXMPP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm uxmpp
.Nd Unix Style XMPP Utilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cm Generic Form:
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl h Ar bare_xmpp_host
.Op Fl p Ar password
.Op Fl u Ar user_jid
.Op Fl v
.Ar command_mode
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Fl h Ar bare_xmpp_host
.Op Fl p Ar password
.Op Fl u Ar user_jid
.Cm disco
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Fl m Ar muc_jid
.Op Fl u Ar user_jid
.Cm bot
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Utilities for XMPP services: 
.Nm
is a utility comprising of a set of 
tools for testing, configuring, troubleshooting, and or using various
XMPP services from a terminal.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Enable debug messages to stderr
.It Fl h Ar bare_xmpp_host
Specify a bare xmpp hostname. For example:
.Cm xmpp.example.com .
.It Fl p Ar password
Specify a password. You should know it is widely accepted as a bad idea to
provide credentials in this manner; I would certainly raise an eyebrow if a
person used this option corresponding to a JID with privileges. That said, you
do you.
.It Fl u Ar user_jid
Specify a user JID. Certain actions, such as the
.Cm disco
command, require s2s connections that are made on behalf of the
applicable
.Ar user_jid .
The password may be provided at the subsequent prompt (best option). If
you like to live dangerously however, you may do so by setting the
.Ev XMPP_PASSWORD
environment variable, or by supplying the password via the
.Fl p
option.
.It Fl v
Print version and exit
.El
.Pp
Other than
.Fl v 
One of the following
.Cm Command Modes
are required in order to actually do anything 
.Qq useful . 
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm disco
Perform a host disco(very) on
.Ar bare_xmpp_host
using a
.Ar user_jid
corresponding to an active user JID of the target host or of another provider
that may federate with the target host.
.It Cm bot
Connect to a given provider, join a MUC, and handle stanzas.
.El
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XMPP_JID
If set, this value will be used as the
.Ar user_jid .
If the
.Fl j
option is specified, this is ignored.
.It Ev XMPP_PASSWORD
If set this value will be used during authentication. 
.Pp
CAUTION:
It is exceedingly easy for other programs running in your environment to read 
this variable as such, like the
.Fl p
option, it should only be used in special cases.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Rs
libstrophe XMPP client library:
https://strophe.im
.El
